{%- comment -%} Getting here (adapted from contact-find-us, without its map): the address, then four ways to come. {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="bg-base-100 text-base-content">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[80rem] px-5 py-20 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-end" data-reveal>
      <div class="lg:col-span-6">
        <p class="eyebrow text-base-content/75">Getting here</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2rem,2.6vw+1rem,3.25rem)]">The barn at the top of the hill</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8">
        <address class="text-[1.1875rem] not-italic leading-relaxed">3471 South Kettle Road<br>Lake Leelanau, Michigan&nbsp;49653</address>
        <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/search?query=Lake%20Leelanau%2C%20Michigan" class="text-link mt-2 inline-block font-semibold" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Get directions</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-300 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4" data-reveal="stagger">
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6"><h3 class="text-[1.375rem]">By car</h3><p class="body-copy mt-2">Twenty-five minutes north-west of Traverse City on M-22, then up South Kettle Road. Park in the lot by the barn.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6"><h3 class="text-[1.375rem]">By bike</h3><p class="body-copy mt-2">The Leelanau Trail passes three miles east. There's a rack by the porch and water at the bar.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6"><h3 class="text-[1.375rem]">With a driver or a tour</h3><p class="body-copy mt-2">Tour buses and limousines by appointment only: call us a week ahead.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-base-100 p-6"><h3 class="text-[1.375rem]">Access</h3><p class="body-copy mt-2">A step-free door and restroom in the barn. The hill walk is on grass and gravel.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
